@startuml
title Word (.docx) Accessibility Pipeline using C#, Mammoth, Playwright, and axe-core

autonumber
skinparam BoxPadding 10

actor "User / System" as User
participant "C# Orchestrator" as App
box "Step 1: OpenXML Prep" #LightBlue
    participant "DocumentFormat.OpenXml" as OpenXML
end box
box "Step 2: HTML Bridge & Validation" #LightGreen
    participant "Mammoth (.NET)" as Mammoth
    participant "Playwright (Chromium)" as Browser
    participant "axe-core (JS)" as Axe
end box

User -> App : Provide input.docx
activate App

== Phase 1: Tag & Convert to HTML ==
App -> OpenXML : Open input.docx
activate OpenXML
OpenXML -> OpenXML : Inject tracking IDs / inspect structure
OpenXML --> App : Return prepared stream
deactivate OpenXML

App -> Mammoth : Convert .docx stream to semantic HTML
activate Mammoth
Mammoth --> App : Return clean HTML string
deactivate Mammoth

== Phase 2: Headless Render & axe-core Audit ==
App -> Browser : Launch headless browser & load HTML
activate Browser
Browser -> Axe : Inject axe.min.js & run axe.run()
activate Axe
Axe -> Axe : Evaluate DOM & computed CSS rules
Axe --> Browser : Return JSON Violation Report
deactivate Axe
Browser --> App : Return parsed violations
deactivate Browser

== Phase 3: Remediate Original OpenXML ==
loop For each accessibility violation
    App -> OpenXML : Locate target node (e.g., <wp:docPr>, <w:tblPr>)
    activate OpenXML
    OpenXML -> OpenXML : Patch XML attributes (e.g., add alt text, <w:tblHeader/>)
    deactivate OpenXML
end

App -> OpenXML : Save changes to fixed_output.docx
App --> User : Return remediated .docx + Audit Report
deactivate App

@enduml
